# Trivy vulnerability ignore list.
#
# Add entries here only for confirmed false positives or vulnerabilities that
# are genuinely not exploitable in this image (e.g. the vulnerable code path is
# never reached). Do NOT use this file to silence real findings — CRITICAL
# severities fail the "docker" CI job by design (see .github/workflows/ci.yml).
#
# Format: one CVE (or GHSA) ID per line, optionally with a trailing comment.
# Example:
# CVE-2023-12345 # base-image glibc CVE, not reachable — process never parses untrusted locale data

# --- Spring Framework 6.2.19: no open-source fix on the Spring Boot 3.5 line -----------
# Both are fixed only in Spring Framework 7.0.9 (Spring Boot 4.x). They are the same two
# CVEs, accepted on the same grounds and until the same date, as in
# dependency-check-suppressions.xml, which records the check behind each claim. They are
# listed here as well because Trivy rates them CRITICAL and gates on them independently.
# Do not extend a date without re-verifying the claim.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2026-12-31 # XsltView RCE: needs view rendering; this app renders no views (JSON @RestControllers only, no template engine)
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2026-12-31 # SSE stream corruption with view fragments: this app exposes no Server-Sent Events endpoints
